            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "bq. Doesn't MMap automatically consume a lot more memory?\n\nNo.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2010-12-20T14:34:13.668+0000",
          "updated": "2010-12-20T14:34:13.668+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12493669/comment/12973213",
          "id": "12973213",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "bq. Doesn't MMap automatically consume a lot more memory?\n\nNo, it consumes *address space*, this is why it only works without problems on 64 bit. The index files are mapped into address space, so handled like a SWAP file, that's the trick. They only consume as much memory from cache space as the operating system decides. Especially it does not consume memory from java heap!\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2010-12-20T14:35:36.531+0000",
          "updated": "2010-12-20T14:41:35.520+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12493669/comment/12973260",
          "id": "12973260",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "There could be a number of things that could make this very OS dependent:\n - kernel read-ahead can differ between mmap and traditional IO, and differ between operating systems\n   (think about reading 10 bytes from position 4094... if mmap doesn't read-ahead at least one page then you will suffer a double page fault).\n - CPU cache / TLB effects?  Using more address space isn't completely free.\n - Java mmap overhead - you don't get access to a raw byte[]\n - userspace-kernel transition times (i.e. for a read system call) differ between operating systems.  Linux is very good here, probably leading to less of a penalty for read vs mmap.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2010-12-20T17:14:15.621+0000",
          "updated": "2010-12-20T17:14:15.621+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12493669/comment/12973264",
          "id": "12973264",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
